+//! Multicore worker, backed by rayon.
+//!
+//! Patched for Uragan. Upstream used a futures ThreadPool for `compute`
+//! and crossbeam scoped threads for `scope`; both create OS threads with
+//! `std::thread::spawn`, which cannot exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown. rayon
+//! lets the embedder supply the threads (`ThreadPoolBuilder::spawn_handler`),
+//! so this same code runs natively -- rayon spawns OS threads -- and in wasm,
+//! where the host starts Node worker_threads over shared memory.
+//!
+//! Only scheduling changes. Every caller and all field/curve arithmetic are
+//! untouched: callers all use `scope.spawn(move |_| ...)` and ignore the
+//! returned handle, which a `rayon::Scope` satisfies as-is. Output does not
+//! depend on the thread count -- field arithmetic is exact -- so a proof for a
+//! fixed seed is byte-identical however many threads computed it.
+//!
+//! Callers must not `wait()` from inside a task (a blocked worker could starve
+//! the pool); bellman only waits on the thread that called `create_proof`.
 
